cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you refer to this work, please cite this repository. It documents a course
  project submitted by a group of four, and credit for the underlying work
  belongs to all four authors listed below.
title: >-
  Operational load forecasting: a foundation model as a known-future covariate,
  and the evidence for every part of the system around it
abstract: >-
  336-hour-ahead forecasting of an operational load index across 96 hourly series
  with 22 covariates, graded by WAPE. The central result is that a frozen,
  zero-shot Chronos-2 scores worse than the supervised Temporal Fusion
  Transformer it advises, yet its forecast handed to that model as a known-future
  covariate is worth +8.1 percent relative, seed-averaged — the largest single step measured
  here. The same foundation model was measured in all three of the roles it can
  take, and gives a different answer in each. Around that, a convex blend of the
  five-seed checkpoint-averaged cascade, a fully fine-tuned copy of the same
  foundation model, and a LightGBM booster, plus two panel-level corrections. The
  repository ships the measured negative results alongside the wins, under a
  gapped cross-validation protocol that mirrors the private split and an
  admission bar built on a paired cluster bootstrap.
type: software
